  <item>
    <title>Extreme Drought Covers 44% of Puerto Rico: Report</title>
    <link>https://www.carriermanagement.com/news/2026/09/04/291705.htm</link>
    <description>Puerto Rico’s normally rainy season has instead brought a severe and fast-growing drought, according to data from the NASA Earth Observatory. Just three months earlier, none of Puerto Rico was classified as being in drought, and less than 20 percent of the territory was considered abnormally dry. By August 25, three-quarters of the territory was in at least moderate drought, with extreme drought covering 44 percent and some areas receiving less than 20 percent of the usual rainfall.</description>
    <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:15:37 +0000</pubDate>
    <guid>https://www.carriermanagement.com/news/2026/09/04/291705.htm</guid>
    <category>General</category>
  </item>
