  <item>
    <title>Use record reinsurance and third-party capital to drive growth, Aon urges insurers</title>
    <link>https://www.artemis.bm/news/use-record-reinsurance-and-third-party-capital-to-drive-growth-aon-urges-insurers/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=use-record-reinsurance-and-third-party-capital-to-drive-growth-aon-urges-insurers</link>
    <description>Broking giant Aon has today urged its insurer clients to leverage the record levels of reinsurance and third-party or insurance-linked securities capital as a growth-driver, saying creative use of capital and access to all its forms is increasingly important. With a record $800 billion of reinsurance capital at June 30th 2026, a new high $144.5 billion of that being from third-party or alternative sources , Aon believes the opportunity is there for protection buyers to harness this abundance to fuel their future growth. Adding that, “As market conditions evolve, product value, capital relief and access to third-party capital are becoming increasingly important.” Aon notes that there are three priorities for reinsurance buyers, using capital creatively to support growth, aligning their risk with capital and product strategies and accelerating performance through faster, more informed decision making.</description>
    <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:15:21 +0000</pubDate>
    <guid>https://www.artemis.bm/news/use-record-reinsurance-and-third-party-capital-to-drive-growth-aon-urges-insurers/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=use-record-reinsurance-and-third-party-capital-to-drive-growth-aon-urges-insurers</guid>
    <category>General</category>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Bermuda re/insurers incur $1.34tn in global gross claims over a decade: BMA</title>
    <link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/bermuda-re-insurers-incur-1-34tn-in-global-gross-claims-over-a-decade-bma/</link>
    <description>Craig Swan, BMA Chief Executive Officer, said: “Incurring US$1.34 trillion in claims and policyholder benefits over a single decade is a striking measure of the financial strength and resilience of the Bermuda market—but beyond the numbers, this milestone represents something far more significant: a testament to promises kept to individuals, businesses and vulnerable communities in their moment of need. Data drawn from Bermuda Monetary Authority (BMA) statutory filings and periodic claims surveys, reveals that the market’s reach accelerated sharply toward the close of the decade, with 2025 alone accounting for 19% of the ten-year total. Accounting for 62% of all claims and policyholder benefits over the decade, the United States formed the largest share of payments by a substantial margin, totalling US$827 billion.</description>
    <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:15:21 +0000</pubDate>
    <guid>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/bermuda-re-insurers-incur-1-34tn-in-global-gross-claims-over-a-decade-bma/</guid>
    <category>General</category>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>East Texas Grapples With Flooding From Tropical Storm Edouard</title>
    <link>https://www.insurancejournal.com/news/southcentral/2026/09/04/884109.htm</link>
    <description>Texas authorities rescued dozens of people from stranded cars, homes surrounded by floodwaters and an assisted living facility as former Tropical Storm Edouard lingered over rural parts of the state and dumped nearly 2 feet of rain in some places. Heavy rains from the storm, which weakened into a tropical depression after making landfall Tuesday, were expected to threaten the eastern part of the state through Thursday morning, the National Weather Service said. In Texas’ hard-hit Hardin County, about 85 miles (137 kilometers) northeast of Houston, officials said flooding, downed trees and powerlines, debris, and power outages were still creating hazardous conditions.</description>
    <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:15:20 +0000</pubDate>
    <guid>https://www.insurancejournal.com/news/southcentral/2026/09/04/884109.htm</guid>
    <category>General</category>
  </item>
