    <title>Ross Fire Continues Burning in North Texas</title>
    <link>https://www.insurancejournal.com/news/southcentral/2026/09/04/884112.htm</link>
    <description>Ten days since the Ross Fire broke out west of Fort Worth, responders are still battling one of the largest wildfires in North Texas’ recorded history. “The fire is estimated at 90,000 acres so there are going to be portions that may see rain, portions that may not see rain,” Laura Stevens, a public information officer with the Texas A&amp;M Forest Service said on Sept. 3 press conference, Texas Division of Emergency Management Chief Nim Kidd said he expected it to take up to two more weeks to fully extinguish the fire.</description>
    <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:15:20 +0000</pubDate>
