    <title>FBI Investigating Possible Exposure of Millions of American IDs</title>
    <link>https://www.insurancejournal.com/news/national/2026/09/04/884088.htm</link>
    <description>The FBI is investigating a potential breach of an ID verification company that may have exposed scans of millions of Americans’ driver’s licenses, a bureau spokesperson told Bloomberg News on Thursday. Access to the data of more than 160 million “North American” driver’s licenses is being sold on a new service called Nexus, according to an advertisement on the Russian-language cybercrime forum known as Exploit. If confirmed, the breach would represent one of the biggest leaks of US government identity documents ever, said Zach Edwards, an American cyber threat researcher, whose identification was among the cache of documents for sale.</description>
