    <description>Lockton Insurance is among companies named in the NBA’s investigation into the Los Angeles Clippers’ circumvention of league salary cap rules to sign star Kawhi Leonard. Clippers president of business operations Gillian Zucker connected Robertson with Kansas City-based Lockton and two other companies, Boingo and Daktronics, in early July 2020, according to an investigation by law firm Watchell, Lipton, Rosen &amp; Katz. Leonard and his then-business partner, Dennis Robertson, violated the league’s circumvention rules by pressuring the Clippers to assist the multiple time All-Star in securing off-court business deals, according to the NBA.</description>
