    <title>Federal Judge Cautions State Farm Against Gambling With Courts</title>
    <link>https://www.claimsjournal.com/news/national/2026/09/04/339968.htm</link>
    <description>A federal judge in Alabama has likened State Farm to a gambler and warned that the insurer’s apparent strategy of trying to move claims litigation from state to federal court is a risky bet that might not be worth taking. The judge remanded the case back to the county court, declaring that there was no “objectively reasonable basis for seeking removal.” The 53 Alabama citizens insured by State Farm filed a 73-count complaint for alleged negligent procurement, fraudulent misrepresentation, and breach of contract against State Farm and 18 insurance agencies and agents. In seeking removal of the case to federal court, State Farm alleged that the plaintiffs had improperly included negligent procurement claims against Alabama agents in their complaint purely to keep the case in state court.</description>
