    <title>Reinsurers likely to be more disciplined at Jan 1 than in past soft markets: Storr, Antares</title>
    <link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/reinsurers-likely-to-be-more-disciplined-at-jan-1-than-in-past-soft-markets-storr-antares/</link>
    <description>Ahead of the 68th edition of the Monte Carlo Rendez-Vous (RVS), Mat Storr, Head of Reinsurance at Antares Global, has said that the upcoming renewals are likely to be more disciplined than in past soft markets. Reinsurers remain disciplined and are far more focused on portfolio quality than simply deploying capital.” Storr continued, “Those relying on optimistic assumptions, weaker governance or insufficient exposure controls may find reinsurers becoming increasingly selective. Storr expects an orderly renewal rather than a dramatic shift in pricing, and anticipates that buyers with well-performing portfolios, strong underwriting discipline, transparent data, and consistent performance could secure more favourable outcomes.</description>
